  "content": "Repo layout is flat at the root — no cmd/ directory. main.go, app.go, api.go (deleted, see DI memory), install.go, stdio.go, config_writer.go all live at repo root in package main; frontend/ and internal/ are top-level dirs. The desktop server is the single binary `yullu` built from `go build .` (not `./cmd/app`). Frontend embeds via `//go:embed all:frontend/dist`. Stdio MCP is a `yullu stdio` subcommand, not a separate binary. Why: simplifies the project, removes Wails-era cruft, makes the entry obvious. `cmd/` was deleted entirely; any reference to `cmd/internal/...` import paths is stale.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"architecture\", \"layout\", \"go\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
